According to Article 13 of the Ghanaian Constitution, a person shall not be held to have deprived another person of their life in contravention of the law if the other person dies as a result of:

1. A lawful act of war; or
2. The use of force to an extent reasonably justifiable in the particular circumstances for any of the following purposes:
   (a) For the defense of any person from violence or for the defense of property;
   (b) To effect a lawful arrest or to prevent the escape of a person lawfully detained;
   (c) For the purposes of suppressing a riot, insurrection, or mutiny;
   (d) To prevent the commission of a crime by that person (Article 13, Chapter 5, p.33).

According to Article 267, revenue from stool lands is distributed as follows:

- 10% of the revenue is paid to the Office of the Administrator of Stool Lands to cover administrative expenses.
- The remaining 90% is disbursed in these proportions:
  (a) 25% to the stool through the traditional authority for the maintenance of the stool in keeping with its status;
  (b) 20% to the traditional authority;
  (c) 55% to the District Assembly within the area of authority where the stool lands are situated (p.173).
